5.) COOKIES AND SESSIONS


Cookies and sessions are used to maintain state between multiple HTTP requests because HTTP itself is stateless.

 COOKIES

A cookie is a small piece of data stored on the client's/browser's side.

HOW COOKIES WORK 

Client / Browser
      │
      │  Login Request
      ▼
    Server
      │
      │  Set-Cookie
      ▼
Client / Browser
      │
      │  Stores Cookie
      │
      │  Sends Cookie with future requests
      ▼
    Server

Example
Set-Cookie: username=Arnav;

The browser stores:

username = Arnav

On the next request, it may send:

Cookie: username=Arnav
Uses of Cookies
Remembering login/session information
Storing user preferences
Shopping carts
Tracking user activity
Remembering website 

 SESSIONS

A session stores user-related information on the server side.

Usually, the browser stores only a session ID, which allows the server to find the user's session data.

HOW SESSIONS WORK 

Client / Browser
      │
      │ Login
      ▼
    Server
      │
      │ Creates Session
      │
      │ Session ID
      ▼
Client / Browser
      │
      │ Stores Session ID
      │
      │ Sends Session ID
      ▼
    Server
      │
      │ Finds session data
      ▼
  User's Data

Example

Server stores:

Session ID: ABC123
User: Arnav
Logged in: Yes
Role: Student

Browser stores only:

Session ID = ABC123

KEY DIFFERENCE 

Cookie = Data stored on the client/browser.

Session = Data stored on the server, identified by a session ID.


COOKIE
Client → Stores Data

SESSION
Client → Stores ID
Server → Stores Data

